# --- synthetic ties -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Three ordering claims in the ruleset are GUARDS rather than fixes for an observed
# misfiling: no cached log exhibits the tie, so moving the rule reclassifies nothing and
# the claim would be an untested assertion. Each therefore gets a constructed fixture, and
# each is labelled synthetic so nobody reads it as measured evidence.
#
# 27 vs 3/10: the guard line in a window that ALSO carries a class-10 aux-file line.
CFLAGS_GUARD_PLUS_AUX = CFLAGS_GUARD.replace(
    "all done\n", "configure.ac:33: error: required file 'ltmain.sh' not found\nall done\n")
# 2 vs 30: a compiler that is absent says so, and that names the cause where class 28 only
# says "read config.log". Class 2 must take the tie.
CONFIGURE_NO_EXE_BECAUSE_NO_GCC = CONFIGURE_NO_EXE.replace(
    "checking whether the C compiler works... no\n",
    "checking whether the C compiler works... no\n./configure: line 2: gcc: command not found\n")
# 35 vs 20: a genuine link failure in a window that also carries haikuporter's resolve
# wording must never be re-filed as a dependency problem -- the #486 mistake, one class up.
UNDEF_REF_PLUS_RESOLVE = UNDEF_REF.replace(
    "collect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status\n",
    "collect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status\n"
